BUT in the Barra Velha  microbial macrostructures which resemble classical stromatolites are rare ( 0.5 of thickness of logged sections)  as are microbial planar laminites ( 1 )  and oncoids ( 0.1 )  Within the key textural components such as shrubs microbial microstructures are very rare with as few as 0.05 to 0.1 of shrubs showing features such as microbial filament moulds In addition – No modern lacustrine carbonate systems produce large differentiated platforms and seismic-scale clinoforms No analogues are currently known from the geological record of lakes There are examples of isolated, sub-lacustrine and subaerial mounds, the former at least of seismic-scale
